# Cloudflare header rules. Honoured by both Pages and Workers static assets;
# this site is currently served by Workers.
# Hashed asset paths and vendored fonts never change contents, so they can be
# cached indefinitely. HTML must revalidate so a new article appears immediately.

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Security headers for every response.
#
# Strict-Transport-Security: refuse plain HTTP for a year once a browser has
#   seen this over HTTPS. Deliberately no `preload` — that submits the domain to
#   a list baked into browser binaries and removal takes months. Its own
#   decision, not a side effect of adding a header.
# Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: "allow-popups" rather than "same-origin", because
#   signing in to comments opens a GitHub OAuth popup and the strict value
#   severs its link to this window.
# Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: social cards and the feed are meant to be
#   fetched from elsewhere.
#
# Content-Security-Policy is appended to THIS block at build time by
# integrations/csp.mjs. Only one rule block may match a path — a second "/*"
# block replaces this one rather than adding to it.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), interest-cohort=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
